@@ -74,7 +74,32 @@ ### Ticket
 - Source queue — the ticket belongs to **one** queue (within the entity); does not record which totem it came from.
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
 - Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
-- Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Issuance channel: `totem`, `virtual` or `printed` (default `virtual`).
+- Status: `waiting` (on issuance) or `called`. There is no cancelled status.
+- Display code (see below).
+
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to one entity and has a `name`, a `slug` (unique within the entity), an `is_active` flag (default `true`) and optional `labels_i18n` (per-locale labels). Tickets can only be issued into **active** queues.
+
+### Issuance
+
+Implemented by `App\Actions\IssueTicket` (`__invoke(Queue $queue, int $priority = 0, TicketChannel $channel = TicketChannel::Virtual): Ticket`):
+
+- The queue row is locked and its `is_active` state is read **from the database** inside the transaction, never from the model instance the caller holds: a queue deactivated after being loaded is still rejected with `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`, and nothing is persisted.
+- A negative priority is rejected with `InvalidArgumentException`.
+- The new ticket is `waiting`, with `issued_at = now()`.
+- A collision on the unique `(queue_id, code)` (concurrent issuance) is retried a few times, each attempt in its own transaction.
+
+### Display code
+
+Per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, ... (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero padded; beyond 999 it grows: `A1000`, `A1001`). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`. `Ticket::nextCode($queueId)` returns the **last valid code by insertion order, plus one** (so `A999` then `A1000` yields `A1001`, not string order). Numbers are not reused when a middle ticket is deleted (`A001..A003` with `A002` deleted → `A004`). Malformed legacy codes (not `A<digits>`) are skipped: only `A-X` → next is `A001`; `A001` then `A-X` → next is `A002`.
+
+### Immutability and single call
+
+After issuance every ticket field is immutable except `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`): an Eloquent save/update that changes any other field (e.g. `code`, `priority`) throws `LogicException`. Bulk query-builder updates bypass model events and must not be used on tickets.
+
+`Ticket::call(User $user)` calls a ticket exactly once: it marks it `called` and records `called_at` and the calling user. Only **members of the ticket's entity** may call (any role); others get `Illuminate\Auth\Access\AuthorizationException` and the ticket is unchanged. Calling a non-waiting ticket throws `LogicException`. The ticket state is re-read under a row lock, so two concurrent calls cannot both succeed. Choosing *which* ticket to call next (priority/fairness) is not implemented yet.
 
 ### Priority
 
